ceert het werk van Frida Kahlo in samenhang met de ervaringen die haar schilderkunst vormgaven. Lichamelijk letsel, ziekte, haar huwelijk en politieke overtuigingen keren op verschillende manieren in de beelden terug. Vooral zelfportretten bieden een toegang tot die persoonlijke wereld. Het boek kijkt daarbij niet alleen naar biografische gebeurtenissen, maar ook naar de eigen beeldtaal waarmee Kahlo ze verwerkte. Zo ontstaat een overzicht van een kunstenaar die haar leven actief tot onderwerp van schilderkunst maakte.","work_id":987122007,"evidence":[{"note":"Exact2010Volkskrant/Taschen9789461060037: KBp327436182 and Bibliotheek317320165 explicitly identify Dutch translationWilBoesten/redactionElkeDoelman. Short cover/spine Kahlo/FridaKahlo is the same full bibliographic FridaKahlo1907-1954:leed en hartstocht, not another biography. Bol English/other-binding conflicts; explicit exactISBN library translation/language and independent physicalhardcover listing take precedence, no title-only language inference.","type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p327436182"],"reference":"work:5183","checked_at":"2026-11-02T22:05:23.248Z","canonical_name_resolution":null},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","review":"content-review-032.json","sources":["https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.317320165.html/frida-kahlo-1907-1954/","https://www.boekwinkeltjes.nl/b/244597931/Kahlo/","https://openlibrary.org/works/OL6224977W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p327436182"]},{"type":"cover_front_review","sha256":"7967e446551d9d2768a228f9e4c9b2b6bb80db5bf8e982c2da8fbfa75e8fa5db","cover_id":9246145,"reference":"cover-semantic-review-003.json","limitation":"Front credits Andrea Kettenmann, Frida Kahlo is subject, not author. Artist biography identity must remain distinct."}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_reviewed_summary","source_url":"https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.317320165.html/frida-kahlo-1907-1954/","reviewed_at":"2026-11-02T22:05:23.248+00:00","source_name":"Gecontroleerde boek- en catalogusbronnen","source_type":"official_catalog","review_batch":"nl-scale-20261102-023","review_status":"approved","bound_author_id":987322003},"before_row":null},{"key":{"edition_id":987222009},"seq":15,"relation":"catalog_edition_metadata","after_row":{"format":"hardcover","work_id":987122007,"evidence":[{"note":"Exact2010Volkskrant/Taschen9789461060037: KBp327436182 and Bibliotheek317320165 explicitly identify Dutch translationWilBoesten/redactionElkeDoelman. Short cover/spine Kahlo/FridaKahlo is the same full bibliographic FridaKahlo1907-1954:leed en hartstocht, not another biography. Bol English/other-binding conflicts; explicit exactISBN library translation/language and independent physicalhardcover listing take precedence, no title-only language inference.","type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p327436182"],"reference":"work:5183","checked_at":"2026-11-02T22:05:23.248Z","canonical_name_resolution":null},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","review":"content-review-032.json","sources":["https://www.bibliotheek.nl/catalogus/titel.317320165.html/frida-kahlo-1907-1954/","https://www.boekwinkeltjes.nl/b/244597931/Kahlo/","https://openlibrary.org/works/OL6224977W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p327436182"]},{"type":"cover_front_review","sha256":"7967e446551d9d2768a228f9e4c9b2b6bb80db5bf8e982c2da8fbfa75e8fa5db","cover_id":9246145,"reference":"cover-semantic-review-003.json","limitation":"Front credits Andrea Kettenmann, Frida Kahlo is subject, not author. Artist biography identity must remain distinct."}],"cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9246145-L.jpg?default=false","edition_id":987222009,"bound_title":"Frida Kahlo","reviewed_at":"2026-11-02T22:05:23.248+00:00","bound_isbn13":"9789461060037","evidence_url":"https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p327436182","review_batch":"nl-scale-20261102-023","review_status":"approved","bound_language":"dut","card_cover_url":"https://covers.openlibrary.org/b/id/9246145-M.jpg?default=false","bound_author_id":987322003},"before_row":null},{"key":{"work_id":987122004,"language":"nl"},"seq":16,"relation":"catalog_work_descriptions","after_row":{"text":"Ruby Landry groeit op bij haar grootouders in de bayou en droomt ervan schilder te worden. Haar gevoelens voor Paul Tate botsen met de afkeuring van zijn rijke familie. Over haar eigen ouders weet zij weinig, totdat een oude foto nieuwe vragen oproept. Wat daarna aan het licht komt, dwingt haar buiten de vertrouwde omgeving naar antwoorden te zoeken. In New Orleans wacht een familiegeschiedenis die haar hoop op erkenning ingewikkelder maakt. Dit eerste Landry-deel volgt Ruby tussen herinneringen aan thuis en een onzekere afkomst.","work_id":987122004,"evidence":[{"note":"Reuse RubyWork2973 and exact Dutch DeKern1994hardcover9789032504403. KB statement explicitly credits VirginiaAndrews/translatorParmaVanLoon; primary publisher credits V.C.Andrews for Landry#1. Estate/byline credit is not sole-personal-authorship proof. Do not attach to AllThatGlitters9216 or merge parents.","type":"reviewed_identity_and_bibliography","sources":["http://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p119769344"],"reference":"work:2973","checked_at":"2026-11-02T22:05:23.248Z","canonical_name_resolution":null},{"type":"original_substantive_source_review","review":"content-review-025.json","sources":["https://www.simonandschuster.com/books/Ruby/V-C-Andrews/Landry/9781982150532","https://knihobot.cz/g/8903789","https://openlibrary.org/works/OL134875W","https://data.bibliotheken.nl/id/nbt/p119769344"]},{"type":"cover_front_review","sha256":"bcbd64c96ecd39a3a8080c654b105c9caaa89837aa0c4d36a12ee044b7e4589a","cover_id":12377658,"reference":"cover-semantic-review-003.json","limitation":"Front and source-edition binding; no barcode or exact-printing-year assertion."}],"language":"nl","provenance":"original_source_revie